{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 7.6,
   "text": "A company spent an estimated three hundred million dollars on a cable from Chicago to New Jersey, just to save three milliseconds."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 7.699,
   "end": 13.614,
   "text": "You see, when a price moves in Chicago, the fastest traders in New Jersey can react before their rivals."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 13.713,
   "end": 19.809,
   "text": "It sounded crazy, until the line made the round trip in about thirteen milliseconds, the fastest route yet."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 20.146,
   "end": 21.728,
   "text": "It looked set for years."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 21.827,
   "end": 26.522,
   "text": "Then microwave towers beat it, because signals fly faster through air than through glass."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 26.621,
   "end": 32.069,
   "text": "In twenty seventeen, the company behind it agreed to sell for one hundred twenty-seven million dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 32.407,
   "end": 39.28,
   "text": "Now Cboe gives traders connecting in two New Jersey data centers the same length of cable, so nobody's wire is shorter."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 39.617,
   "end": 45.272,
   "text": "It's a race measured in milliseconds, and if you hold stocks for years, you never had to run it."
  }
